{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevTailBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevTailBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevArgmax","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LobTaylorSaddle","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TrapezoidRule","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianSumBound","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_le_argmax_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_le_argmax_mul","kind":"theorem","line":1046,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L1046-L1091","doc":"**`⟨4₁⟩_N ≤ g_{k*}·C(N,w)`**, with `C` an explicit expression and no\nthreshold on `N`.\n\nEvery summand of `C` is `O(√N)` or better: `w/N² ≤ 1/N`; the `D`-term is\n`≈ 36√3/π ≈ 20` at `D ≈ N/6`; the two window terms are the `√N`.  Collapsing\n`C` to a single numeral needs `√3 ≤ 1.8`, `π ≥ 3.14` and a threshold — which is\nexactly what this statement avoids, at the cost of being longer to read. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_below_window_le_argmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_below_window_le_argmax","kind":"theorem","line":1014,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L1014-L1042","doc":"**The below-window region, against the peak.**  Everything below the secant\nwindow costs at most `g_{k*}·(w/N² + w√3N/(πD(D−1)))`, `D = k*−w`.\n\nBoth summands are `O(1)`: `w ≤ N` makes the first `≤ 1/N`, and `D ≈ N/6` makes\nthe second `≈ 36√3/π ≈ 20`.  Stated with `D` explicit rather than collapsed to a\nnumeral, so no threshold on `N` is smuggled in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.max_one_kashaevProd_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.max_one_kashaevProd_le","kind":"theorem","line":958,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L958-L1012","doc":"The endpoint value that dominates the below-window region, against the\npeak: `max 1 g_w ≤ g_{k*}·(1/N² + √3N/(πD(D−1)))`, `D = k*−w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.exp_neg_le_one_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.exp_neg_le_one_div","kind":"theorem","line":953,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L953-L956","doc":"`e^{−x} ≤ 1/x` for `x > 0` — from `x + 1 ≤ e^x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_le_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_le_split","kind":"theorem","line":931,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L931-L938","doc":"`⟨4₁⟩_N` bounded above by the three regions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_kashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_kashaev","kind":"theorem","line":925,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L925-L929","doc":"`⟨4₁⟩_N ≥ e^{−1}·m·g_{k*}` when `√3πm² ≤ N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd","kind":"theorem","line":888,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L888-L917","doc":"**The whole sum, from below.**  `⟨4₁⟩_N ≥ e^{−1}·m·g_{k*}` whenever\n`√3·π·m² ≤ N`; taking `m ≈ √(N/(√3π))` makes that `≥ c√N·g_{k*}`.\n\nNearly free once `sum_kashaevProd_Icc_eq` exists: the window sum is a sub-sum of\nthe whole sum and every term is nonnegative.  Unlike the upper bound, this needs\nNO region decomposition — dropping terms only helps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_le_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_le_split","kind":"theorem","line":838,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L838-L886","doc":"**The three regions, recombined.**  An exact split of `Finset.range N` into\n`[0, w)`, `[w, k*]` and `(k*, N)`, each bounded by the corresponding lemma.\n\nEvery piece here is sorry-free, but the first summand is `O(N)·max 1 g_w`, NOT\n`O(√N)·g_{k*}` — collapsing it needs the numeric constant recorded in the bean\n(`e^{−x} ≤ 1/x` against `D = k*−w ≈ N/6`, threshold `N ≥ 62`).  So this is a\nbound on `⟨4₁⟩_N` in three named pieces, not the `C√N·g_{k*}` statement.\n\n`hw2` is `2N + 3 ≤ 3w`, one step stricter than the secant window's `2N ≤ 3w`:\nthe middle region here is the CLOSED `[w, k*]`, so the distance-indexed sum runs\nto `d = k*−w`, which lands at `w` — and the window has to hold there too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_Icc_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_Icc_eq","kind":"theorem","line":823,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L823-L836","doc":"The distance-indexed window sum IS the interval sum, reflected. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_left_of_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_left_of_sq","kind":"theorem","line":793,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L793-L814","doc":"**The `√N` from below.**  When `√3·π·m² ≤ N` the last term is `≥ e^{−1}`, so\nthe window sum is at least `e^{−1}·m·g_{k*}`.  Taking `m ≈ √(N/(√3π))` makes\nthat `≥ c√N·g_{k*}` — the matching side of `sum_kashaevProd_right_le`.\n\nThe caller chooses `m`; picking it as an explicit floor-of-a-square-root is\nNat arithmetic that would obscure the one inequality doing the work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_left","kind":"theorem","line":755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L755-L791","doc":"**Lower bound for the window sum**, the mirror of\n`sum_kashaevProd_left_window_le`.  Every term is at least the last. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_ge_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_ge_left","kind":"theorem","line":668,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L668-L745","doc":"**Lower bound below the saddle.**  `g_{k*−d} ≥ g_{k*}·exp(−√3π d(d+1)/N)`,\nfor every `d ≤ k*`.\n\nNote `d(d+1)`, not `d(d−1)`: bounding from below costs one step more than\nbounding from above, because the `d`-th step back is at most `(d+1)h` from `θ*`\nrather than at least `(d−1)h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sq_le_kashaevProd_argmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sq_le_kashaevProd_argmax","kind":"theorem","line":638,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L638-L652","doc":"`N² ≤ kashaevProd N ⌊5N/6⌋` — the peak dominates the exact endpoint value\n`kashaevProd N (N−1) = N²`.  Sharper than `one_le_kashaevProd_argmax`, and it\nis what makes the `k ≤ N/6` terms (each `≤ 1`) negligible against the peak. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_below_window_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_below_window_le","kind":"theorem","line":620,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L620-L636","doc":"**The whole region below the secant window is at most `w · max 1 g_w`.**\n\nThat is `O(N)` times an endpoint value, not `O(√N)` times the peak — but the\nendpoint `g_w` is itself exponentially below the peak (`kashaevProd_left_tail`\nat distance `k* − w ≈ N/6`), so the region contributes `O(1)` relative to\n`g_{k*}` rather than `O(√N)`.  Turning that into a single numeric constant is\narithmetic over `e^{−x} ≤ 1/x` and `N² ≤ g_{k*}`; it is NOT done here, and this\nlemma alone does not bound `⟨4₁⟩_N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_max_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_max_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L601-L618","doc":"Below the window, every term is dominated by an endpoint: `g_k ≤ max 1 g_w`\nfor `k ≤ w ≤ 5N/6`.  `1 = kashaevProd N 0` covers the falling stretch and `g_w`\nthe rising one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_left_window_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_left_window_le","kind":"theorem","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L549-L591","doc":"**The window below the saddle is `O(√N)` times its largest term too.**\n\nStated by DISTANCE `d` from the saddle rather than by index `k`, which is how\n`kashaevProd_left_tail` is indexed — so no reindexing is needed and the\nGaussian sum bound applies directly.  The set `{k* − d : d < m}` is\n`Ico (k*−m+1) (k*+1)`; saying so is not needed to state or use the bound.\n\nThe window hypothesis `2N ≤ 3(k*−m)` is the secant's domain `θ ≥ 2π/3`, so `m`\nreaches about `N/6` — far wider than the `√N` that matters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_right_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_right_le","kind":"theorem","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L517-L547","doc":"**The sum from the saddle upward is `O(√N)` times its largest term.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_left_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_left_tail","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L427-L507","doc":"**The left tail is Gaussian too.**  For `b ≤ 5N/6` and `d` steps back that\nstay above `2π/3`,\n\n    kashaevProd N (b−d) ≤ kashaevProd N b · exp(−π d(d−1)/(√3 N)).\n\nThe step-`d` gain is `θ* − θ_{b−d}`, which is at least `d·h` precisely because\n`b ≤ 5N/6` — the same arithmetic progression as the right tail, run backwards,\nwith `1/√3` in place of `√3` because a secant is shallower than the tangent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_ge_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_ge_exp","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L390-L425","doc":"One step of the left tail: below the saddle the ratio is at least\n`exp(2(θ* − θ)/√3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_log_two_sin_secant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_log_two_sin_secant","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L332-L388","doc":"**Secant bound.**  `log(2 sin θ) ≥ (5π/6 − θ)/√3` on `[2π/3, 5π/6]`.\nThe left-hand counterpart of `log_two_sin_le_tangent`, and the reason the left\ntail is Gaussian too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_two_pi_div_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_two_pi_div_three","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L323-L330","doc":"`cot(2π/3) = −1/√3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_right_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_right_tail","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L239-L313","doc":"**The right tail is Gaussian.**  `kashaevProd N (k*+d) ≤ kashaevProd N k* ·\nexp(−√3 π d(d−1)/N)`.\n\nThe exponent is quadratic in `d` because the tangent bound at `θ*` makes the\nper-step penalty grow LINEARLY: summing an arithmetic progression is where the\n`d²` comes from.  Bounding every factor by the first would give only `e^{−cd/N}`\nand would not confine the sum to a `√N`-window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_exp","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L207-L237","doc":"One step of the right tail: past the saddle the ratio is at most\n`exp(−2√3 (θ − θ*))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_le_tangent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_two_sin_le_tangent","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L120-L203","doc":"**Tangent bound (concavity).**  `log(2 sin θ) ≤ −√3 (θ − 5π/6)` on `(0, π)`.\nEquality exactly at `θ*`; this is the whole source of the right tail's\nGaussian decay. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_antitoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_antitoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevTailBound.lean#L92-L116","doc":"`cot` is antitone on any `[c,d] ⊂ (0, π)`: its derivative is `−csc² < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}